                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "One of my childhood favorites that I never beat but just loved walking/driving around in.  Well child me is definitely proud because I went back and got all the achievements, including a 100% hardcore playthrough where your save deletes if you die.  It's not a very hard game but the collectibles are actually really well-hidden so 100%ing is a real challenge. The real strength here lies in the art direction and how everything is lovingly crafted to be as Australian as possible.  They do a great job making the small environments feel massive and for a GameCube game the scope and variety here is really impressive.  The pseudo open-world was ahead of its time and the wide variety of boomerangs gives you a lot of ways to interact with the world and craft a unique playstyle as you go.\r\n\r\nThis definitely held up much better than I'd expected, but I've got maximum rose-colored glasses for it so I'm far from unbiased.  I really did enjoy my time revisiting this game though, except for the god-awful loader mech sections where you just walk 0.5mph with clicky knees for 5 minutes at a time.",
